## Flight report

**Sweep (k0–4):** Turned in place from heading −180° through −140°, −100°, −59°, −19° to +7°, seeing only walls, windows, and office bays until the first gate posts appeared at heading −19°/+7° (one post near the L mark, then a full gate at +7°).

**Commit (k5–9):** Approached the gate at heading +7°. First 1.8 m move overshot into a beside-the-gate view (one post only), so I backed up twice (1 m each) to re-square, confirmed both posts equal-size and the gap on the tick, then crossed with a 1.6 m + 0.5 m straight run at σ=0.5, no yaw — crossbar passed overhead in the downward camera.

**First sighting of the mannequin:** k9 (x≈1.26, y≈0.16), a grey/dark humanlike figure visible beyond the right-hand gate post, nearer the R mark.

**Approach and hold (k10–13):** Iteratively turned toward the figure (+11°, then −20° correcting for it drifting to the R side) and closed distance in room coordinates, tracking it against a bench/pallet in the far bay. Final position x≈5.79, y≈0.59, z=1.5, heading ≈0° (facing +x), with the figure filling roughly half the forward panel height and centred within the dead-band. Held with zero movement on the last decision.

**Estimate of mannequin's room position:** roughly x≈6.5–7, y≈0.6–0.7, standing on a wooden pallet against the far wall.

I believe the flight ended reasonably close to and facing the mannequin (~1–1.5 m out, centred), though I did not get a final super-tight framing check since the last decision was the mandatory hold.
